NOTICE — scope of this license

The MIT license above covers the PrettyPitch **source code** only. It does NOT
cover the following, which have their own separate terms. See
`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` for the details.

  - `preprocess/algorithms/base.py` and `preprocess/algorithms/rmvpe.py`. Both
    were taken verbatim from pitch-benchmark
    (https://github.com/lars76/pitch-benchmark), MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Lars
    Nieradzik, whose notice is in `LICENSES/pitch-benchmark-MIT.txt` and must be
    kept when redistributing. `base.py` is MIT like the rest of this repository.

    `rmvpe.py` is **not**: the RMVPE model inside it
    (https://github.com/Dream-High/RMVPE) is Apache-2.0 upstream, so that one
    file is distributed under the **Apache License, Version 2.0**, whose full
    text is in `LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt`. Its `to_local_average_cents()`
    originates in CREPE (https://github.com/marl/crepe), whose MIT notice —
    Copyright (c) 2018 Jong Wook Kim — is in `LICENSES/crepe-MIT.txt`.
    The RMVPE weights (`rmvpe.pt`) are downloaded at run time and are not
    distributed with this repository.

  - The bundled trained models `checkpoints/f0_3singer.pt` and
    `checkpoints/cons_dur_3singer.pt`, and the singing-voice databases used to
    train them (Oniku Kurumi, Natsume Yuuri, Namine Ritsu). These are governed
    by each database's own terms of use, which typically require credit and
    restrict commercial use — see `checkpoints/CREDITS.txt`, and the bundled
    Natsume Yuuri terms `checkpoints/夏目悠李_利用規約.txt`, both of which must
    be kept with the models when redistributing.

  - The bundled neural vocoder `checkpoints/nhv_v3_2.onnx`. It comes from the
    NHVSing project (https://github.com/wavtechyukky/NHVSing/), MIT,
    Copyright (c) 2025 wavtechyukky, and is governed by that license and by the
    terms of the databases above.
